# .pii-allow -- real-world identifiers this repo is ALLOWED to contain.
#
# One literal per line, each with a reason. An allowlist entry has to be argued for and shows up in
# the diff -- unlike quietly widening a regex, which is how a guard rots into a rubber stamp.
#
# Legitimate: a third-party CORPORATE sender address that a parser/filter must literally match.
# NEVER legitimate: the operator's own data. If it is theirs, it does not belong in a public repo.

carfax@event.carfax.com               # Gmail filter must literally exclude Carfax submission receipts
carfax@no-reply.carfax.com            # same, Carfax marketing stream
no-reply@accounts.google.com          # Gmail filter must literally exclude Google security notices
sales@dealer-domain.edealerhub.com    # the eDealerHub CRM auto-mail sender pattern the triage table keys on

# Public corporate/vendor phone lines. These ARE the reference's content -- the buyer literally calls
# them. Third-party business numbers, published by the businesses themselves; not personal data.
800-868-7000                          # Subaru Motors Finance lease-cash line (payment_methods.md)
516-983-3800                          # Lemon Protector PPI shop, published line (ppi_booking.md)
718-229-7594                          # Lemon Protector PPI shop, published line (ppi_booking.md)
844-997-3624                          # YourMechanic national PPI booking line (ppi_booking.md)

# PA tax-rate example ZIPs in the state-fee table. Reference data about a state's flat rate, not a
# residence -- the table names three of them side by side.
19010                                 # Bryn Mawr PA, flat-6% example row (state-fee-lookup)
19406                                 # King of Prussia PA, same table
19380                                 # West Chester PA, same table
